# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FarmGrid AI - ignore rules
#
# Everything here is either generated, local-only, or sensitive. Nothing in this
# file is needed to run the project from a fresh clone.
#
# Note on patterns: in .gitignore, `*` does NOT match `/`. A rule like
# `data/models/*.pt` therefore only covers files sitting directly in
# data/models/ - the trained classifier actually lives one level deeper in
# data/models/equipment_classifier/, so it needs `**`. Getting this wrong is how
# a 17 MB model artifact ends up in a commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.example IS committed; the real .env never is.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json

# --- Local database ---------------------------------------------------------
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*

# --- Django generated --------------------------------------------------------
staticfiles/
media/
logs/
*.log

# --- Trained model artifacts (large binaries, rebuildable) --------------------
# These live one or more levels below data/models/, hence **.
data/models/**/*.pt
data/models/**/*.pth
data/models/**/*.onnx
data/models/**/*.joblib
data/models/**/*.pkl
data/models/**/*.h5
data/models/**/*.tflite
data/models/**/*.safetensors
data/models/**/weights/

# --- Fetched / generated data -------------------------------------------------
# Raw ingestion output and its provenance reports: tens of MB, regenerated by
# the data_ingestion management commands. data/seed/ IS committed - seed_platform
# needs it on a fresh clone.
data/ingested/
data/raw/
data/tmp/

# --- Generated documentation dumps -------------------------------------------
# frontend.txt is a one-off snapshot of the templates; the templates themselves
# are the source of truth and this copy would silently go stale.
frontend.txt

# --- Test / coverage / caches -------------------------------------------------
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
.tox/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Editors / OS -------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Node (only used by the ad-hoc tooling in temp; not required to run) ------
node_modules/
package-lock.json
package.json

# --- Local scratch ------------------------------------------------------------
tmp/
scratch/
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej